        <body>
            <div xml:id="d453">

                <pb facs="0678" n="578" xml:id="pg578"/>

                <head>No. 453.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-04-27"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 27, 1884</date>.
                        (Received May 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 907.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 892, of date 10th
                    instant and to my No. 902, of date 18th instant, both relative to the case of
                    Mr. John Dalton, United States consul at Ciudad Bolivar, I have the honor to
                    inclose herewith: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>A printed copy of the letter or order of the President, Guzman Blanco,
                            which I referred to in my No. 892 as the same appears in the <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Opinion Nacional</hi> of the 31st ultimo,
                            together with a translation thereof.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>A copy of the note referred to in my No. 892, of date 1st instant,
                            which I addressed to Mr. Seijas, with a view of preventing the arrest of
                            Mr. Dalton.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>A copy and translation of Mr. Seijas’ note, of date 7th instant, in
                            reply to mine.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>A copy of my note of date 26th instant, in rejoinder to the note of
                            Mr. Seijas.</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>A copy of the dispatch, of date 18th instant, and referred to in my
                            No. 902, which I addressed to Mr. Dalton.</item>
                        <label>6.</label>
                        <item>A copy and translation of a part of Venezuelan law, referred to in Mr.
                            Seijas’ note.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>I, of course, draw the attention of the Department to all of these in-closures
                        <hi rendition="#italic">in extenso.</hi></p>
                <p>My view is that the President’s order is in violation of constitutional
                    guarantees, and especially and plainly in violation of the guarantee relative to
                    ind vidual security.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have still received no communication from Mr. Dalton on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JEHU BAKER.</signed></closer>







